eservation result was measured.","No audio was read or played; no rights-cleared speech, music, or silence cohort, consent record, or output-use grant is present.","No listening panel, target-device timing, resource measurement, benchmark, or release review was performed.","No provider, descriptor, registry, default, installed-v0, ABI, shared-build, CI, board, or handoff file is changed."],"observed_provenance":{"candidate_note":{"algorithm_specified":false,"evidence_class":"source_reported_provenance_not_remeasured","license_reviewed":false,"line":872,"link_line":1034,"measured_result_recorded":false,"network_used_here":false,"not_reproduced_here":true,"path":"cpp-library/pipeline-validation/playback-speed-candidates.md","present":true,"qualifies":false,"recorded_lines":["| Speech actuator, lowest latency | **pbshift** | MIT | C++17, pitch-synchronous voice path, 0.25–4×, automatable rate, Live tier 56–64 ms at 48 kHz (vendor) | Pre-1.0, 2 GitHub stars, self-reported metrics; not independently tested |","**pbshift.** MIT, C++17 static library, streaming pull API (`feed` → `available` → `read`), independent pitch/stretch, rate automatable between `feed()` calls, 0.25–4× (clamped), formant preservation, deterministic output. Its `Voice` path is pitch-synchronous and time-domain, which is the right family for speech; the vendor reports **56 ms (formant) / 64 ms (no formant)** Live latency at 48 kHz, versus ~99–128 ms for Studio-RT. The project is pre-1.0 and effectively unproven, so treat it as a **P0 challenger**, not a dependency to ship without measurement. It vendors a modified Signalsmith Stretch 1.3.2 for its extreme-speech path (MIT) and pffft (BSD-like).","- pbshift — <https://github.com/pbtechlab/pbshift> (MIT; README latency/API; 2026-11-04)"],"runtime_identity_recorded":false,"sha256":"661a471ad50e3335b18fdb6d8664f6fda0534ad37196fb9e3f58ff61c58f34b3","statement":"pbshift is source-reported as an MIT C++17 streaming actuator with pitch-synchronous voice path